# Setting X and Y Coordinates in a Contour Plot

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

`x:` and `y:` can be any numeric lists — they do not need to be uniformly spaced.
Non-uniform coordinates distort the contour shape to reflect real data spacing.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Contour}

# Non-uniform x and y coordinates
x = [0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13]
y = [0, 1, 3, 6, 10]

z = for yi <- 0..4 do
  for xi <- 0..6 do
    :math.sin(xi / 3.0) * :math.cos(yi / 2.0)
  end
end

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(Contour.new(x: x, y: y, z: z))
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Contour Plot with Non-Uniform X and Y Coordinates")
|> Plotly.show()
```
